1
00:01:46,377 --> 00:01:47,962
Wanna try 'em on?

2
00:01:48,546 --> 00:01:50,214
I can't afford it.

3
00:01:50,297 --> 00:01:53,217
Becca gave the nod. All yours, no strings.

4
00:01:54,051 --> 00:01:55,511
No thanks.

5
00:01:55,594 --> 00:01:59,974
Didn't bother you
when you put that klepped Sandy on.

6
00:02:00,057 --> 00:02:03,144
Can't scavenge off someone you knew?

7
00:02:03,227 --> 00:02:05,062
They're techie mitts anyways.

8
00:02:05,146 --> 00:02:07,148
You're just being picky.

9
00:02:07,231 --> 00:02:09,525
I have my sights set on something else.

10
00:02:09,608 --> 00:02:10,901
Wha'tcha got your eyes on?

11
00:02:12,403 --> 00:02:14,405
Oh! This?

12
00:02:14,989 --> 00:02:16,866
Bit big for you, ain't it?

13
00:02:16,949 --> 00:02:18,659
I can handle it.

14
00:02:19,243 --> 00:02:21,745
Sure, all yours if I flatline.

15
00:02:22,246 --> 00:02:25,291
Gives you time to bulk up, grow into 'em.

16
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:28,669
'Kay. Deal.

17
00:02:30,212 --> 00:02:32,756
Ya know, something's different about you…

18
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:33,674
Huh?

19
00:02:34,258 --> 00:02:37,803
You're usually moping,
bringing the vibe down…

20
00:02:37,887 --> 00:02:39,430
Resident buzzkill.

21
00:02:39,513 --> 00:02:42,474
I'm not!
And I ain't no different from yesterday!

22
00:02:42,558 --> 00:02:43,934
Nah. Something's off.

23
00:02:44,518 --> 00:02:46,145
Ya get laid?

24
00:02:47,813 --> 00:02:48,731
You did.

25
00:02:49,523 --> 00:02:52,693
Gotta work on that poker face, son!

26
00:02:52,776 --> 00:02:55,446
Kiwi! Any progress?

27
00:02:55,529 --> 00:02:57,781
Not at all.

28
00:02:59,283 --> 00:03:03,203
Tanaka's beefed up his defenses
since the last gig.

29
00:03:03,871 --> 00:03:06,874
Tried poking holes around,
but it's been a no-go.

30
00:03:06,957 --> 00:03:11,211
What did I tell ya? We ain't getting
nowhere unless Faraday feeds us something.

31
00:03:11,795 --> 00:03:13,172
Tanaka?

32
00:03:13,255 --> 00:03:15,966
Remember your very first grand theft auto?

33
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:17,468
He's the owner of the limo.

34
00:03:19,053 --> 00:03:20,220
Problem?

35
00:03:20,304 --> 00:03:22,014
Nah, it's nothing…

36
00:03:22,097 --> 00:03:23,474
Would you look at that.

37
00:03:23,557 --> 00:03:25,976
You were schoolmates with Tanaka's kid.

38
00:03:27,561 --> 00:03:32,691
What?! You accusing our kid of
going to some stuffy corpo school?!

39
00:03:32,775 --> 00:03:36,737
Bona-fide Arasaka Academy dropout.
Straight A student, too.

40
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:38,739
I'll be damned!

41
00:03:38,822 --> 00:03:43,827
Guess we now know why Gloria was
always strapped on cash.

42
00:03:44,453 --> 00:03:47,498
What's a guy gotta do
to get some privacy around here?

43
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:53,212
There's not much else I could find on
Tanaka's private file. The rest is trash.

44
00:03:53,295 --> 00:03:56,006
-Like?
-XBDs in his viewing log.

45
00:03:56,090 --> 00:03:59,551
That's good. We can use it for leverage.

46
00:03:59,635 --> 00:04:01,762
A real kinkster. More gore than porn.

47
00:04:01,845 --> 00:04:04,098
Some cyberpsycho shit, too.

48
00:04:04,682 --> 00:04:07,017
The deep, dark fetishes of a suit.

49
00:04:08,143 --> 00:04:11,021
Lots of vids from a gonk who goes by JK.

50
00:04:11,105 --> 00:04:11,939
JK?

51
00:04:13,482 --> 00:04:14,650
Heard of him?

52
00:04:14,733 --> 00:04:19,405
Sure. Jimmy Kurosaki. The braindance
director with a cult following.

53
00:04:19,488 --> 00:04:24,785
He's known for putting up snuff reels
within 24 hours of it happening.

54
00:04:24,868 --> 00:04:29,164
Never seen any director
do the edits that he does.

55
00:04:29,248 --> 00:04:32,042
No wonder he's got so many fans.

56
00:04:32,126 --> 00:04:35,087
Didn't know you were a superfreak.

57
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:36,046
Uh, well…

58
00:04:36,130 --> 00:04:39,675
Just helped a choom
move his stock, is all.

59
00:04:39,758 --> 00:04:44,346
That's good and all, but do you have
any intel we can actually use?

60
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:45,639
They're custom-made.

61
00:04:45,723 --> 00:04:46,557
What?

62
00:04:47,141 --> 00:04:51,103
I heard that he sometimes tunes
custom-made footage for VIPs.

63
00:04:51,186 --> 00:04:53,147
You know, like removing pain limiters?

64
00:04:53,230 --> 00:04:54,565
So what?

65
00:04:54,648 --> 00:04:58,902
If he's tuning the footage,
Tanaka's gotta be there as well.

66
00:04:58,986 --> 00:05:00,195
And probably alone.

67
00:05:00,279 --> 00:05:02,072
Alone? How you figure?

68
00:05:02,156 --> 00:05:05,576
Would you bring a bodyguard
to tune up a fetish BD?

69
00:05:07,911 --> 00:05:08,954
Kid's got a point.

70
00:05:09,038 --> 00:05:11,206
Getting sharp, kid!

71
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:14,376
Now that you're a man now!

72
00:05:14,877 --> 00:05:17,463
What? Did something happen?

73
00:05:17,546 --> 00:05:18,714
Nothing!

74
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:22,468
Faraday came through
with a lead on Tanaka.

75
00:05:22,551 --> 00:05:25,846
Seems our favorite suit
occasionally ditches his huscle

76
00:05:25,929 --> 00:05:28,098
and usual ride for a Delamain.

77
00:05:28,182 --> 00:05:30,017
Going off-radar, huh?

78
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:33,812
But Delamain's got him fully covered.
Still can't pinpoint his destination.

79
00:05:33,896 --> 00:05:37,733
I also looked into
the tuning services for BDs.

80
00:05:37,816 --> 00:05:42,321
The main buyers are fat cats,
corpo execs, celebrities, gang bosses…

81
00:05:42,404 --> 00:05:45,074
You get in by referral
and the location is undisclosed.

82
00:05:45,157 --> 00:05:48,285
If we wanna know more,
we'd have to chat with the man himself.

83
00:05:48,368 --> 00:05:49,661
How?

84
00:05:49,745 --> 00:05:51,371
Gotta grab him in person.

85
00:05:51,955 --> 00:05:57,461
Lucky for us, he has a reservation at
Embers tomorrow. He'll be alone.

86
00:05:57,544 --> 00:05:59,379
At a ritzy place like that? Sad.

87
00:05:59,463 --> 00:06:02,883
Great. When he leaves,
let's invite him here for a nightcap.

88
00:06:03,467 --> 00:06:05,302
Let's go.

89
00:06:33,747 --> 00:06:37,543
Hey! You wouldn't happen to be
Jimmy Kurosaki, would you?

90
00:06:39,002 --> 00:06:39,962
Who's asking?

91
00:06:40,045 --> 00:06:42,464
I knew it! I'm a huge fan, sir!

92
00:06:42,548 --> 00:06:46,927
You know a ripperdoc
in Arroyo who pushes XBDs?

93
00:06:47,010 --> 00:06:50,305
I helped him sell your stuff!

94
00:06:50,389 --> 00:06:51,306
Really.

95
00:06:51,390 --> 00:06:53,684
Can I shake your hand?

96
00:06:53,767 --> 00:06:58,689
Oh, sorry… Guess I'm a bit star-struck.

97
00:06:58,772 --> 00:07:00,566
Yeah, I got places to be.

98
00:07:00,649 --> 00:07:03,068
Right… I won't hold you up.

99
00:07:03,152 --> 00:07:05,028
Was an honor meeting you…

100
00:07:14,872 --> 00:07:16,331
What was that?!

101
00:07:20,043 --> 00:07:21,211
Fuck!

102
00:07:22,129 --> 00:07:23,255
What?!

103
00:07:23,839 --> 00:07:25,757
Maine!

104
00:07:26,341 --> 00:07:27,468
Where's David?

105
00:07:27,551 --> 00:07:29,011
Find him!

106
00:07:29,094 --> 00:07:30,637
Snap out of it!

107
00:07:35,851 --> 00:07:37,186
You alright?

108
00:07:37,269 --> 00:07:40,272
Son of a bitch pulled something on us.

109
00:07:41,023 --> 00:07:42,524
What happened?

110
00:07:42,608 --> 00:07:44,359
They're gone.

111
00:07:44,443 --> 00:07:45,277
Gone?

112
00:07:45,903 --> 00:07:48,030
He nabbed David.

113
00:07:49,198 --> 00:07:51,825
Kiwi! You take Maine and head out.

114
00:07:51,909 --> 00:07:53,035
Okay.

115
00:07:53,118 --> 00:07:54,745
I'm fine…

116
00:07:54,828 --> 00:07:56,788
Be a good boy, and stay!

117
00:07:56,872 --> 00:07:59,041
Lucy! You're with me.

118
00:08:07,674 --> 00:08:11,345
Got him. Mile and change, straight ahead.

119
00:08:11,428 --> 00:08:14,014
What did that asshole use back there?

120
00:08:14,097 --> 00:08:15,933
Seemed like some kind of EMP.

121
00:08:16,016 --> 00:08:20,854
It got Kiwi real bad.
Only gave me a bit of a shock.

122
00:08:20,938 --> 00:08:26,109
Neural implant targeting.
To neutralize runners, clearly.

123
00:08:26,693 --> 00:08:27,653
You seem okay.

124
00:08:27,736 --> 00:08:28,737
I wasn't in range.

125
00:08:29,446 --> 00:08:31,490
David could be in real shit.

126
00:08:31,573 --> 00:08:33,867
It'll be a problem if he uses that again.

127
00:08:33,951 --> 00:08:36,245
Not if we kill him first.

128
00:08:37,788 --> 00:08:39,248
You're pissed, aren't ya?

129
00:08:39,831 --> 00:08:41,291
A little.

130
00:09:09,987 --> 00:09:11,530
Ah, fuck.

131
00:09:11,613 --> 00:09:13,740
Think it's a cyberpsycho?

132
00:09:13,824 --> 00:09:18,370
No shit, let's head out.
Already hailed MaxTac.

133
00:09:20,122 --> 00:09:21,540
Hey, there's another body.

134
00:09:22,207 --> 00:09:25,043
Don't wander off, man.
What if you run into them?

135
00:09:25,627 --> 00:09:28,088
Don't worry. They're not around anymore.

136
00:09:29,631 --> 00:09:31,550
Hm? Who's there?!

137
00:09:31,633 --> 00:09:32,884
The cyberpsycho!

138
00:09:32,968 --> 00:09:34,052
He's got a gun!

139
00:09:34,136 --> 00:09:35,637
-It wasn't me…
-Drop the gun!

140
00:09:35,721 --> 00:09:36,847
Don't move!

141
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:39,808
-I woke up and I was just…
-Drop it, you fucking psycho!

142
00:09:43,645 --> 00:09:44,938
Who's there?!

143
00:09:45,022 --> 00:09:46,440
Hey! What happened?!

144
00:09:53,030 --> 00:09:54,615
Got a cyberpsycho!

145
00:09:54,698 --> 00:09:55,657
Raise MaxTac now!

146
00:10:15,218 --> 00:10:17,012
Shots fired back there!

147
00:10:17,679 --> 00:10:19,473
Die, bastard!

148
00:10:57,052 --> 00:10:58,220
MaxTac?!

149
00:11:20,492 --> 00:11:21,743
Fucking monster.

150
00:11:21,827 --> 00:11:23,995
No! It wasn't me!

151
00:11:39,469 --> 00:11:41,096
Awesome, isn't it?

152
00:11:41,179 --> 00:11:44,850
Experiencing your own death
instead of someone else's.

153
00:11:45,517 --> 00:11:47,352
Are you fucking kidding me?!

154
00:11:47,936 --> 00:11:51,773
Awesome? You fucking psychopath…

155
00:11:52,816 --> 00:11:55,735
Hey, I thought you were a fan!

156
00:11:55,819 --> 00:11:58,113
Most of my fans are whack jobs.

157
00:11:58,697 --> 00:12:01,366
You're a cyberpunk, aren't you?

158
00:12:01,950 --> 00:12:03,201
What are you after?

159
00:12:03,285 --> 00:12:05,745
Ambushing me in a place like that…

160
00:12:06,455 --> 00:12:10,625
Clearly, you've done your homework.
Have you seen any of my other works?

161
00:12:10,709 --> 00:12:13,253
The Edgerunner series?

162
00:12:14,045 --> 00:12:15,130
Yeah.

163
00:12:16,047 --> 00:12:18,633
I've seen most of your stuff.

164
00:12:19,342 --> 00:12:21,636
Wow. I'm flattered!

165
00:12:23,930 --> 00:12:29,519
Say, have you ever wondered
where I get those cyberpsycho scrolls?

166
00:12:29,603 --> 00:12:30,812
What?

167
00:12:30,896 --> 00:12:36,776
All military prototypes come with
a built-in braindance scroller.

168
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:42,032
Some people are willing to
pay through the nose for that kinda stuff.

169
00:12:45,243 --> 00:12:48,288
You know who originally owned this Sandy?

170
00:12:48,872 --> 00:12:53,210
James Norris. How many people
did he kill in the end? 27?

171
00:12:53,293 --> 00:12:56,796
Had a hell of a run-in
with MaxTac in the end.

172
00:12:57,464 --> 00:13:02,928
It's not often you get a guy
who can go toe-to-toe with them.

173
00:13:03,011 --> 00:13:07,641
That was so good…
One of the best I've seen in a while.

174
00:13:10,268 --> 00:13:13,647
I've got high expectations for you, too.

175
00:13:13,730 --> 00:13:17,776
I'm surprised you're still sane
after wearing this.

176
00:13:17,859 --> 00:13:21,404
The side-effects are gonna
drive you mad, eventually.

177
00:13:21,488 --> 00:13:23,865
Can't wait to see it.

178
00:13:23,949 --> 00:13:26,409
I'm not gonna go psycho!

179
00:13:26,493 --> 00:13:30,664
That's what all chromers say.

180
00:13:30,747 --> 00:13:33,917
They think they're all sane
until they aren't.

181
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:34,918
Not me!

182
00:13:35,001 --> 00:13:36,419
Yes, you.

183
00:13:37,003 --> 00:13:42,175
Another couple rounds with the MaxTac
and your brain'll burst like a balloon.

184
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:47,764
Wait. You're not gonna
make me go through that again…

185
00:13:49,015 --> 00:13:50,809
Hey, stop!

186
00:13:50,892 --> 00:13:51,935
Cut it out!

187
00:13:52,018 --> 00:13:53,937
Stop!

188
00:13:58,608 --> 00:13:59,484
Don't move!

189
00:14:04,072 --> 00:14:05,490
Put your hands up…

190
00:14:06,074 --> 00:14:07,242
Or you're dead.

191
00:14:07,951 --> 00:14:09,494
You got me!

192
00:14:14,416 --> 00:14:15,250
How's David?

193
00:14:15,333 --> 00:14:17,043
He's in a BD or something.

194
00:14:17,127 --> 00:14:19,004
-Can you get him out?
-I'll try.

195
00:14:19,588 --> 00:14:20,672
Need a hand?

196
00:14:20,755 --> 00:14:21,756
Shut it!

197
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,091
Got it!

198
00:14:27,012 --> 00:14:29,472
David! You alright?

199
00:14:29,556 --> 00:14:31,558
Aw, what a shame.

200
00:14:32,392 --> 00:14:35,020
So? What do you guys want?

201
00:14:35,103 --> 00:14:37,647
I assume you're not here to kill me.

202
00:14:37,731 --> 00:14:39,399
That's still up for jury.

203
00:14:39,482 --> 00:14:42,152
Come on. I'll cooperate.

204
00:14:42,235 --> 00:14:43,778
You catch on quick.

205
00:14:50,243 --> 00:14:52,037
That better not be…

206
00:14:53,997 --> 00:14:55,665
Armed drones!

207
00:14:55,749 --> 00:14:56,666
Bingo!

208
00:14:57,417 --> 00:14:58,460
Call them off!

209
00:14:58,543 --> 00:15:00,253
No can do.

210
00:15:00,337 --> 00:15:04,674
Go on, give 'em a wave.
They're my best toys. Bulletproof and all.

211
00:15:04,758 --> 00:15:08,428
Good luck putting them down
with those tiny little bangers.

212
00:15:08,511 --> 00:15:10,472
I'll blow your brains out first!

213
00:15:10,555 --> 00:15:12,307
Well, that wouldn't be very smart.

214
00:15:12,390 --> 00:15:16,561
That won't stop them from turning you
into a bloodstain on my floor.

215
00:15:16,645 --> 00:15:20,690
Yeah? They won't shoot as long as
I'm using you as a meat-shield.

216
00:15:24,069 --> 00:15:26,529
Knew it was smart to have two.

217
00:15:26,613 --> 00:15:27,572
Shit!

218
00:15:28,156 --> 00:15:30,241
Oh no! Looks like you're surrounded.

219
00:15:30,325 --> 00:15:31,868
Ready to give up?

220
00:15:31,952 --> 00:15:33,161
Shut up!

221
00:15:33,244 --> 00:15:34,079
Lucy!

222
00:15:34,162 --> 00:15:35,830
On it…

223
00:15:38,583 --> 00:15:39,709
I need more time…

224
00:15:45,799 --> 00:15:46,633
David!

225
00:15:46,716 --> 00:15:48,218
I'll distract them!

226
00:15:54,182 --> 00:15:55,350
Hurry it up, Lucy!

227
00:16:23,378 --> 00:16:25,213
Wow! That was impressive!

228
00:16:25,296 --> 00:16:26,923
-Mother…
-Fucker!

229
00:16:27,674 --> 00:16:31,052
White flag! White flag!
Okay, I surrender for real this time!

230
00:16:31,136 --> 00:16:32,846
White flag my ass!

231
00:16:32,929 --> 00:16:35,432
You're already dead, shit stain!

232
00:16:35,515 --> 00:16:38,435
I mean, alright, but I thought
you wanted to ask me things?

233
00:16:38,518 --> 00:16:39,686
God dammit!

234
00:16:39,769 --> 00:16:45,358
Hey girl! Takes real talent
to pull off a hack so quickly.

235
00:16:46,526 --> 00:16:49,946
I'll listen to what you have to say,
but can I get up, please?

236
00:16:50,030 --> 00:16:52,782
No funny business or I'll kill you myself.

237
00:16:52,866 --> 00:16:54,909
I won't. Pinky swear.

238
00:16:56,244 --> 00:16:59,205
Alright. Everyone got the plan?

239
00:16:59,289 --> 00:17:01,624
Aye aye, captain.

240
00:17:01,708 --> 00:17:04,711
I'll call you later.
Until then, stay here.

241
00:17:05,378 --> 00:17:08,506
Keep an eye on him.
Don't let him out of your sight.

242
00:17:16,306 --> 00:17:18,224
Sorry about earlier.

243
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:19,726
Whatever.

244
00:17:20,393 --> 00:17:23,063
Didn't think you'd agree
to help us so easily.

245
00:17:23,563 --> 00:17:29,444
I know how cyberpunks work.
I don't really have a choice, do I?

246
00:17:30,028 --> 00:17:30,987
Well, yeah.

247
00:17:32,238 --> 00:17:34,074
You've seen that one too?

248
00:17:34,157 --> 00:17:34,991
Yeah.

249
00:17:35,075 --> 00:17:37,952
You saw it
and you still installed the Sandy?

250
00:17:38,036 --> 00:17:39,746
You're one crazy dude.

251
00:17:39,829 --> 00:17:42,499
I won't end up like him.

252
00:17:42,582 --> 00:17:46,377
James Norris was a soldier
who knew his way around implants.

253
00:17:46,461 --> 00:17:49,089
But even he couldn't take it
and went psycho.

254
00:17:49,672 --> 00:17:52,467
What makes you think you're different?

255
00:17:53,218 --> 00:17:56,721
I don't know. It just… feels right.

256
00:17:57,263 --> 00:17:59,849
It's like the implant's
always been a part of me.

257
00:18:00,683 --> 00:18:03,978
I think… I'm built different.

258
00:18:04,562 --> 00:18:06,815
You think you're special?

259
00:18:06,898 --> 00:18:07,732
Sure.

260
00:18:10,819 --> 00:18:14,447
I've seen plenty of chromejocks
go psycho over the years.

261
00:18:14,531 --> 00:18:17,659
Some metal's simply not meant to
mix with meat.

262
00:18:17,742 --> 00:18:23,748
Your organic body, your soul, gets pushed
to the edge. Teeters on the brink.

263
00:18:24,332 --> 00:18:26,751
It always comes down to one of two things.

264
00:18:26,835 --> 00:18:29,254
You either lose your mind…

265
00:18:29,838 --> 00:18:32,006
Or die… No in-between.

266
00:18:40,098 --> 00:18:43,268
We will be arriving
at the destination shortly.

267
00:18:44,978 --> 00:18:48,731
As requested, the record of
your ride today has been expunged.

268
00:18:48,815 --> 00:18:50,984
I look forward to serving you again.

269
00:18:53,236 --> 00:18:57,490
Hey, Mister Tanaka. Come on in.

270
00:18:59,284 --> 00:19:01,452
You're early.

271
00:19:01,536 --> 00:19:04,289
It usually takes months for a new release.

272
00:19:04,372 --> 00:19:08,793
Well, it's difficult finding
good material, you see.

273
00:19:08,877 --> 00:19:12,255
But this next one'll be worth your while.

274
00:19:12,338 --> 00:19:15,300
Would you like to have it
tuned immediately?

275
00:19:15,383 --> 00:19:18,303
My son is being discharged
from the hospital tonight.

276
00:19:18,386 --> 00:19:20,763
I will just be taking the chip.

277
00:19:21,556 --> 00:19:23,057
I see.

278
00:19:23,725 --> 00:19:26,686
That's unfortunate. I'm proud of
how this one turned out.

279
00:19:26,769 --> 00:19:29,814
It'd be a huge waste not to have it tuned.

280
00:19:29,898 --> 00:19:32,066
The sensitivity'd be off the charts.

281
00:19:32,150 --> 00:19:33,568
Mister Kurosaki.

282
00:19:33,651 --> 00:19:35,528
I do not humor slow men.

283
00:19:35,612 --> 00:19:37,322
Unfortunate's one word for it.

284
00:19:37,947 --> 00:19:42,827
Would've made our job a lot easier
if you were in that BD.

285
00:19:43,411 --> 00:19:44,412
Who are you?

286
00:19:44,495 --> 00:19:45,872
Don't try nothing.

287
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:49,083
The nerve…

288
00:19:49,167 --> 00:19:52,337
Super sorry, sir.
They have me by the balls.

289
00:19:52,420 --> 00:19:55,548
Do you have any idea
who you're dealing with?

290
00:19:58,426 --> 00:20:02,096
Forget about the panic button.
We've got a jammer up.

291
00:20:05,058 --> 00:20:06,851
Just as planned, I see.

292
00:20:15,568 --> 00:20:16,694
Not fucking now!

293
00:20:25,995 --> 00:20:26,955
Maine!

294
00:20:30,458 --> 00:20:31,376
You're…

295
00:20:37,674 --> 00:20:39,842
Pain in my ass.

296
00:20:46,724 --> 00:20:48,101
Must've been the needles.

297
00:20:48,184 --> 00:20:49,352
Got him in the neck.

298
00:20:49,435 --> 00:20:50,895
Shit, he really was slow.

299
00:20:50,979 --> 00:20:52,897
He's suffocating.

300
00:20:52,981 --> 00:20:54,649
Ah… Sucks for him.

301
00:20:54,732 --> 00:20:58,903
Looks like he won't be around
to edit his own death scroll.

302
00:21:08,079 --> 00:21:09,163
Flatlined.

303
00:21:10,248 --> 00:21:12,417
Shit. Trauma Team's coming.

304
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:15,044
What? This bitch had Trauma coverage?

305
00:21:15,128 --> 00:21:17,797
Yup. Platinum and everything.

306
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:18,923
Fuck.

307
00:21:20,842 --> 00:21:22,677
Kid, we're getting the hell out!

308
00:21:22,760 --> 00:21:25,430
Now. They find us and we're fucked.
